# Build context filter (audit STR-02 / SEC-02).
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` shipped the whole working tree into the builder
# stage: the git history, every Markdown document, the coverage profile and the
# agent scratch directories. None of it is compiled, all of it invalidates the
# layer cache on every edit, and anything that lands in the context can end up
# in an image layer.
#
# Note the consequence for versioning: .git is excluded, so `git describe`
# cannot run inside the build. Version, commit and build date are passed in as
# build arguments instead — see the Dockerfile header.

# Version control and CI metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Build outputs and generated profiles
build/
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.prof
*.test
*.exe

# Documentation and audit trail (not compiled)
docs/
*.md
# LICENSE and NOTICE stay in the context: the image ships them (EVAL-01).

# Local tooling and agent state
.claude/
.devcontainer/
.vscode/
.idea/
.env
.understand-anything/

# Container definitions themselves
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
